[
    {
        "content": "<p>I tried to use the induction tactic with <code>fg_induction</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Submodule</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hT</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">FG</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">something_complicated</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">induction</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">using</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fg_induction</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">generalizing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- can do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- can do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hN</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hT</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- fails, no access to hT</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I managed to do this eventually using <code>apply</code> with <code>revert S</code> (I struggled for a while on the revert part):</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">revert</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fg_induction</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hT</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- can do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- can do</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>But isn't the induction tactic designed to handle precisely this? I searched mathlib, and wherever I found <code>fg_induction</code> it got used with apply or refine, never with the induction tactic. Is there maybe something wrong with <code>fg_induction</code>? I could fix it as part of <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/37484\">#37484</a>.</p>",
        "id": 583006899,
        "sender_full_name": "Martin Winter",
        "timestamp": 1775041066
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>the motive of <code>fg_induction</code> should depend on the fg hypothesis</p>",
        "id": 583009903,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1775042033
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Can you explain what you mean precisely? I am not familiar with the \"motive\" terminology. Does this mean <code>fg_induction</code> needs fixing, or am I using it wrong?</p>",
        "id": 583015909,
        "sender_full_name": "Martin Winter",
        "timestamp": 1775043859
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>\"motive\" is computer science speak for \"the statement of the thing you're proving\". Does <code>revert hT</code> before induction help? Or also generalise hT?</p>",
        "id": 583032204,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1775048305
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>it needs fixing but there's a better way to fix it than what you've put in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/37484\">#37484</a></p>",
        "id": 583034777,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1775048923
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Currently my PR does not attempt to fix this problem. But if you tell me how to do it I can include this in the PR.</p>",
        "id": 583036661,
        "sender_full_name": "Martin Winter",
        "timestamp": 1775049437
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"110038\">Kevin Buzzard</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Problem.20using.20induction.20on.20.60fg_induction.60/near/583032204\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Does <code>revert hT</code> before induction help? Or also generalise hT?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I can't generalize hT. </p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Unnecessary <code>generalizing</code> argument: Variable <code>hT</code> is generalized automatically</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>And even with <code>revert hT</code>, the hypothesis hT is not available in the last branch.</p>",
        "id": 583038378,
        "sender_full_name": "Martin Winter",
        "timestamp": 1775049862
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>you would want to change <code>(P : Submodule R M → Prop)</code> to <code>{motive : (N : Submodule R M) → N.FG → Prop}</code> in the type of <code>fg_induction</code></p>",
        "id": 583103668,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1775066726
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Like this?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fg_induction</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Submodule</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">FG</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">singleton</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∙</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">fg_span_singleton</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">sup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">N₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Submodule</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hN₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N₁</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">FG</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hN₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N₂</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">FG</span><span class=\"o\">),</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hN₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hN₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">N₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N₂</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hN₁</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hN₂</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Submodule</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hN</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">FG</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hN</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Submodule</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hT</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">FG</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">something_complicated</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">induction</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hT</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">using</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fg_induction</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">generalizing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">singleton</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hT₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hT₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 583138335,
        "sender_full_name": "Martin Winter",
        "timestamp": 1775079456
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>yeah like that, except it should be an implicit argument and it should be called <code>motive</code></p>",
